,title,link,text,language,family
0,Churahi - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Churahi,"Churahi (Takri: 𑚏𑚰𑚤𑚭𑚩𑚯) is a Western Pahari language of Himachal Pradesh, India. It is spoken in the Chaurah and Saluni tehsils of Chamba district, and is considered endangered.",Churahi,Indo-European
1,Indo-European languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indo-European_languages,"The Indo-European family is significant to the field of historical linguistics as it possesses the second-longest recorded history of any known family after Egyptian and the Semitic languages, which belong to the Afroasiatic language family.",Churahi,Indo-European
2,Anki | Latest Churahi Song 2025 | Shivansh Abrol | Pooja ...YouTube MusicChurahi - WikipediaIndo-European Music - playlist by kinoid | SpotifyChurahi - JioSaavn - Listen to New & Old Indian & English ...Sanjeev Churahi - Apple MusicIndo-European languages - Wikipedia,https://music.youtube.com/watch?v=3z4EF0E2Tdc,"Here we present another Churahi Folk Melody, ""Anki"" Do subscribe for updates... Credits: Singers: Shivansh Abrol & Pooja Vashisht Music/ Video Direction: ... Up next Lyrics Related Playing from Churahi Mashup - चुराही मैशप- DJ Blast | Mehar Singh | New Pahari Folk Music Mix Save Autoplay Add similar content to the end of the queue Churahi (Takri: 𑚏𑚰𑚤𑚭𑚩𑚯) is a Western Pahari language of Himachal Pradesh, India. It is spoken in the Chaurah and Saluni tehsils of Chamba district, and is considered endangered. Indo-European Music · Playlist · 485 songs · 19 likes Listen to Churahi on the music album Churahi by Rajeev Jaryal, only on JioSaavn. Play online or download to listen offline - in HD audio, only on JioSaavn. Listen to music by Sanjeev Churahi on Apple Music. Find top songs and albums by Sanjeev Churahi including Laaldeiye, Barkha Ra Pala and more. The Indo-European family is significant to the field of historical linguistics as it possesses the second-longest recorded history of any known family after Egyptian and the Semitic languages, which belong to the Afroasiatic language family. Where are Indo-European languages spoken? Historically, Indo-European languages were also spoken in Anatolia and Northwestern China. Are all Indo-European languages derived from a single prehistoric language? All Indo-European languages are descended from a single prehistoric language, linguistically reconstructed as Proto-Indo-European, spoken sometime during the Neolithic or early Bronze Age (c. 3300 – c. 1200 BC). Where did the word Indo-European come from? Thomas Young first used the term ""Indo-European"" in 1813, deriving it from the geographical extremes of the language family: from Western Europe to North India. A synonym is Indo-Germanic (Idg. or IdG.), specifying the family's southeasternmost and northwesternmost branches. What languages are in the Indo-European family? The Indo-European family is divided into several branches or sub-families, including Albanian, Armenian, Balto-Slavic, Celtic, Germanic, Hellenic, Indo-Iranian, and Italic, all of which contain present-day living languages, as well as two major extinct branches, Anatolian and Tocharian.",Churahi,Indo-European
